WEBVTT

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.580
You're such a slowpoke, Rita.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.040
Alright, everyone, stay where you are and listen.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:36.290
We have some new workers
joining us here at the laundry mill today.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.580
Now, ladies, if you'd introduce yourselves...

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:41.580
I'm Bea...

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.040
Becky!

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.130
Dorothea.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.380
I'm Chieko.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.710
My name is Priscilla.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.830
Quit staring at me, would ya?!

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:58.580
It's Alice.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.250
Anyone disrespects me...

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.750
And I knock 'em to Kingdom Come!

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:03.540
Hey!

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.250
What kind of a cover is that?

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:10.540
I'm a former delinquent who decided to
turn over a new leaf when her mother fell ill,

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.630
So I went to work, but I can't hide my bad attitude.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:15.080
That's an elaborate backstory.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.670
It's the optimal cover for this mission.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.420
Right. The mission.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.750
Poison Gas Jack.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.210
An elusive phantom killer who's been making
a name for himself in the tabloids.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.670
He's been assassinating important people
who've shown support for the Commonwealth.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:05.710
But we haven't identified any backers.
We believe he's working alone.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.000
Then we have but to exterminate him.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.040
I will handle it.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.250
A man who uses poison gas will be an easy opponent.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.790
We'll have to find him first.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.880
I wonder what he's trying to accomplish.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.330
Look at this.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.670
This is nerve gas, isn't it?

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:28.210
I thought production of nerve gas
was banned by the Geneva Convention.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:29.420
Precisely.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:32.830
So where did he get his illegal poison?

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.920
Getting the ingredients would be difficult, too.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.830
Which means he's in the Army?

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.080
Control had the same idea.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:44.670
Gas produced before the Convention
is lying unused in military storehouses.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.500
You mean inside the London Wall?

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:48.630
Yes.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.540
The storehouses were built
before the second round of construction,

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:54.460
So you'd have to go through
the military barracks to get to them.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:58.830
The odds are good that our poisoner
lives in those barracks.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:00.920
How many are housed there?

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.420
About 1200.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:03.710
That many?!

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.670
How will we find him?

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.920
Disguise ourselves as soldiers?

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.830
No, the Army is a boys' club.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.330
Women would draw too much attention.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.330
And living in the barracks alongside them,

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.880
it would be difficult to maintain a manly facade.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.460
Then what do we do?

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:21.250
Men don't do laundry.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:22.250
What?

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.750
That's true.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.130
None of the boys in class-

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.420
Of course!

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.880
Nerve gas would adhere to his clothes.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.540
And the barracks send all of the men's uniforms
to a laundry mill for washing.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:41.710
So we infiltrate the laundry mill
and find the uniform that reacts to a pyridine test.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.080
This is going to take some time.

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:54.000
Um, Miss Alice, you can't just
move the desk around without-

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.130
I don't like being ordered around!

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:58.500
Go away!

00:04:58.500 --> 00:04:59.710
Y-yes, ma'am!

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.580
So that's what she meant by "optimal cover."

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.920
It does keep people from asking questions.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:14.290
By the way, Your Highness, why did you come along?

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.500
I'm a part of the team, too!

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:19.460
Listen to you talk.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.630
You just wanted to see what it was like, didn't you?

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:22.960
Yes, I did!

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.880
This may be a foolish question, but...

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.920
Who is the master laundress of this establishment?

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:29.830
Master?

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:31.830
That would have to be Marilla.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.000
Many pardons.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:38.000
I've heard that you have the greatest skill with the iron.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.630
I request your guidance.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.420
Stand next to me.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:42.710
First, watch.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:45.880
Then if you have any questions, just ask.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:49.750
You have my thanks.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.920
Japanese people are odd.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.670
I guess I can't expect to find it that soon.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.710
Still...

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.500
Someone turn it off!

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:20.540
I think that's all for this one.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.460
Guess it's time for a break.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.080
But we haven't been working an hour.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.830
Hooray! Break time!

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.790
Let's have some lunch!

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.000
Really!

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.170
Let's go!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.000
In two days, we've tested
a total of 150 articles of clothing.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:44.210
But we couldn't confirm a single reaction
to our chemical test.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:47.040
At this rate, it's gonna take us a month.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.750
Those women are all too lazy!

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.000
If they would work harder, they could earn more!

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:54.540
You're very strict, aren't you, Miss Chise?

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.710
Heave-ho.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.210
Huh?

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.790
Guess it's about time for a break.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.210
Whew!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.710
So much work today.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.920
Put down the iron, Japan Girl.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.920
No, thank you. I am not tired.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:34.170
You may all rest without me.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.540
Take a break! That's the rule!

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.830
You have but one life to live!

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:48.830
Why would you not give everything your best effort?

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.250
Hey! I'm trying-

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.130
Rita!

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:05.080
Are you alright?

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.040
Yes.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.540
Thank you for your help.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:10.790
These scars...

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.960
This is why I told you to take a break!

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:15.170
The machinery here is junk!

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:19.040
If we don't give it a rest every so often, people get hurt.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.500
We get paid by the day.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:23.460
If we get hurt, we can't earn any money.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:26.750
We may not like it, but we do what we can to get on.

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.040
Is the foreman in?

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:33.250
Pwah.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:37.250
You rabble. I don't care who,
but one of you get the foreman.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.130
Tell him Franky is here. He'll understand.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.880
Surely you are aware, Foreman,

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.540
that your payment is due.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:47.750
Y-yes, of course.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.040
So what will it be?

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.920
If you can't pay, then I'll run
your sorry little mill into the ground.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:53.880
Are you ready for that?

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.880
No, I need a little...

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:57.920
Is he going to close the mill?

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:59.040
He can't!

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.290
Are we bankrupt?

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:03.630
I always said that foreman was useless as a manager!

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:04.670
What do we do?

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:06.040
I don't know.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.130
That's going to put a damper on our plans.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:08.460
Are we even going to be paid this month?

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:11.080
I didn't know this place was in debt.
Are we even going to be paid this month?

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:12.630
What do we do?

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:15.290
Mother's surgery is at the end of the month.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:18.000
Chise, don't.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.080
Why not?

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:23.380
If you can't pay now, when can you?

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:24.710
H-hey!

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:26.670
Pardon me.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.670
What do you want?

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.080
How do you do, everyone?

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.130
What? Who are you?

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:34.420
We're in the middle of an important discussion!

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:38.460
I know. And I've come with an important proposal.

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:43.170
I'm going to buy this laundry mill.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:44.040
Huh?

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.040
What...

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:47.420
And I will pay off the debt.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:49.670
That should resolve all the problems, shouldn't it?

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:51.880
Stay out of this, little girl!

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:54.080
We're not playing a game here!

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:57.380
Y-you would really buy the mill, debt and all?

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.210
Yes. I would.

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:02.540
Stop making up stories! A woman, buying the mill!

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:03.630
Who do you think you-

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:04.500
Ow! Oww!

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:05.750
That hurts!

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.710
Don't you dare raise your hand against a lady,
you piece of garbage!

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:09.880
Boss!

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.880
Don't be such a pigheaded jackass!

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:16.790
No, stop!

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.920
She says she's gonna buy the mill,

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:20.380
so shut up and sell it to her, dammit!

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:23.880
Come on, what are you even doing?

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:30.630
What were you thinking,
buying a mill that's losing money?

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:35.250
If the laundry mill were to close,
that would be the end of our mission, wouldn't it?

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:38.540
We just need two more weeks
to check all of the soldiers' uniforms.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:41.920
And we need to keep the mill
in business until then, is that it?

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.750
But Princess...

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:47.670
You don't have that much money
at your disposal, do you?

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.750
I'm surprised you knew that.

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:54.960
But I don't intend to let the laundry mill
be a poor investment.

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:57.710
You intend to make a profit from it?

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:59.040
Yes!

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.080
Impossible! Not from that place!

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:03.460
That isn't like you, Miss Chise.

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:06.750
I thought we could do anything
with hard work and practice, right?

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:08.130
But...

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:11.540
What about you, Ange? Do you think it's impossible?

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:14.000
Nothing is impossible for a spy.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:16.080
Don't you lie to us.

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:25.290
The machines here have always made
such terrible noises.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:28.670
I don't think they've ever seen proper maintenance.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.750
I'd believe that from that stingy foreman.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:36.710
I think if we just fix them up right,
they'll be able to work that much harder for us.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:38.670
And the accidents will cease?

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:39.710
Yes!

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:42.380
All we have to do is replace the old parts,
and it will be fine!

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:46.080
We should rearrange them, too.

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:48.170
The workpath is too convoluted.

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:50.880
If we line the machines up according to work sequence,

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:52.750
we can save ourselves a lot of running around.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:56.580
I imagine they placed them
in order of when they were purchased.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:58.580
They do look heavy.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.540
I can change that weight to zero.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.790
Then I order you as foreman.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:07.250
Rearrange the machinery to create
the optimal work path.

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:10.170
Right, and we'll get all the tools
organized while we're at it.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.790
Some of the girls can't read,
so let's have pictures on the signs.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.420
Let's repair these pipes, too.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:20.000
Princess, may we try the method used in my country?

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:22.500
Sounds fascinating! Tell me about it!

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:28.790
What happened here?

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:30.960
It's so organized.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.580
The belts have stopped squeaking.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:39.750
It's like a new machine!

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:41.580
We serviced them!

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:45.710
Some dust got mixed in with the old grease,
and clogged it up.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:49.250
We cleaned it, so it won't stop anymore.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:51.880
Wait, YOU girls did all this?

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.380
Yes.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:54.460
In one night?

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:56.710
Yes, in one night.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.540
And so, everyone.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.790
Today we'll have a fresh start, and work our hardest!

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:06.250
This is easy!

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.380
So fast!

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:17.830
Ugh!

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:19.790
May I have a word?

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:22.630
We know an excellent way to do laundry.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:24.540
Miss Chieko.

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:32.920
When we're sad, we'll all laugh

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:34.880
We want to go see our mothers and fathers

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:36.920
What's that song?
We want to go see our mothers and fathers

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:37.920
It's coming from the laundry mill.
We want to go see our mothers and fathers

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:38.830
It's coming from the laundry mill.
When we want to cry, we'll all laugh

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:39.830
When we want to cry, we'll all laugh

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:40.880
It's an odd song.
When we want to cry, we'll all laugh

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.500
When we want to cry, we'll all laugh

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:48.330
So we can cry tears of joy

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:51.830
So we can

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:53.250
We're done.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:54.750
For the whole week.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:13:59.830
We did it!

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:00.880
I don't believe it!

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:02.670
We finished so fast!

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:04.380
Ahem.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:06.170
Ladies of the laundry mill!

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:08.630
Now that we've improved our efficiency,

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:11.170
I don't suppose you'd like to improve
our revenue, as well?

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:13.710
What? You mean earn more money?

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.830
If we wash more, we earn more.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:18.790
But there's nothing left to wash,

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:21.540
And the Army won't bring more 'round til the weekend.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:24.170
Then we'll just have to get some from other sources.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:27.500
Some of you girls could really shine with a little polish.

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:28.880
What?

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:34.250
Hey! Keep lollygagging
and it'll be dark before we're through!

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:38.790
Hello!

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:41.040
I'm here with a business proposal.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:42.920
What kind of proposal?

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:46.630
We would like to wash all of your work clothes.

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:47.830
"We"?

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:50.960
We look forward to working with you!

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:52.040
With you!

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.290
Me, too!

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:54.040
You sure are cute!

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:55.040
Oh, bother.

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.540
We already have a launderer.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.880
But you can change that!

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:01.500
Boss!

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.880
Let's let them wash our clothes!

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:06.290
Weren't you just complaining about their sloppy work?

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:07.460
You boys...

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:10.500
I suppose we could see how you do.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:12.710
Hooray!

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:32.920
That's an awful lot of clothes.

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:36.630
We had a lot of success,
thanks to our excellent saleslady.

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:39.790
What? Rita?

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.460
Yoohoo!

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:44.670
What happened?

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.420
You're all so pretty, I hardly recognize you!

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:50.290
Miss Dorothea taught us how to wear makeup.

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:51.630
What! Lucky!

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:52.460
No fair!
Do me, too!

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:53.250
Me, too!

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:57.710
Alright, save the chatter.

00:15:57.710 --> 00:15:59.880
Let's get these clothes in the machines.

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:01.580
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:05.670
Thanks for doing sales, Rita.

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:07.130
Yeah!

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:09.710
What's this report?

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:13.580
It's the income and expense report
for the laundry mill Princess purchased.

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:18.080
They've increased revenue 231% since last year.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.000
Ho ho, how interesting.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.000
What the hell are they doing?

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:25.170
I thought their job was to find Poison Gas Jack!

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:27.460
Wasting their time on these frivolities!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.290
What does D say about it?

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:33.170
That it was a necessary measure
in continuing the mission.

00:16:56.420 --> 00:16:58.290
Where's my uniform?

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:00.250
I left it on my bed.

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:05.000
Oh, is that all? They came around collecting laundry,
so I gave it to them for you.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:11.130
It's just, this guy always does his own laundry!

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:12.880
He didn't want your help, Mate.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.330
What? Have to do it the way Mummy taught you?

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:19.580
Turn one more round

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:21.960
Let's do our best to earn a living

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:27.290
To eat delicious food

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:32.670
When we're tired, we'll all sing

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:35.290
So we can stop our sighing

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:36.880
You can use this if you wish.
So we can stop our sighing

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:37.130
So we can stop our sighing

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:38.080
Uh, thanks.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.420
Uh, thanks.
When we're sad, we'll all laugh

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:41.710
When we're sad, we'll all laugh

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:42.830
A bandage?
When we're sad, we'll all laugh

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:43.540
You wear it like this.
When we're sad, we'll all laugh

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:43.880
You wear it like this.
We want to go see our mothers and fathers

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:47.500
We want to go see our mothers and fathers

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.460
It's called a hachimaki.
We want to go see our mothers and fathers

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:48.880
When we want to cry, we'll all laugh

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:52.080
In my country, we use them to rouse our fighting spirit.
When we want to cry, we'll all laugh

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:53.420
I see.
When we want to cry, we'll all laugh

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:53.960
When we want to cry, we'll all laugh

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:59.290
So we can cry tears of joy.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:15.540
Miss Dorothy!

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:18.630
What's up?

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:19.670
Look.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:22.630
That's our Princess.

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:24.420
You have a way of attracting things.

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:29.710
Private William Ricard, Platoon 2.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:33.580
His unit's barracks is right above the storehouse.

00:18:33.790 --> 00:18:35.130
Then he's the one?

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:37.500
Yeah. I'll go get the car.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.330
Put the evidence in this bag.

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:40.630
All right.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:56.920
You.

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:59.080
What are you doing here?

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:03.710
None who work here feel the need
to walk with such cat-like tread.

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:05.290
And...

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:13.000
Scoundrel.

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:26.880
Hello? Chieko!

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:34.330
Marilla!

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:37.170
Long live the Kingdom!

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:37.830
NO!

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:48.290
I was...

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:50.210
Um...

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:13.170
Miss Chieko and the others
haven't come to work in days.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:16.040
You don't think they have tummyaches, do you?

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:20.750
Ladies, would you all come here, please?

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:23.920
What is it? Why are we having a meeting?

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:26.750
Are our wages going up again?

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:30.580
I've decided to step down as foreman.

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:32.130
What?!

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:34.130
Why? We need you!

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:35.290
Tell us why!

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.830
What happened to Chieko?

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:40.210
Are ALL of you quitting?

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:41.290
No!

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:46.250
I still have so much to learn! Don't go!

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:48.130
They didn't even say goodbye!

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:51.040
Stay with us forever, Priscilla!

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:52.420
All of you, be quiet!

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.960
We've had people quit before, remember?

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:58.830
I'm sure they have their reasons.

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:00.880
Thank you, Marilla.

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:05.040
It's nothing. Forcing you to stay
would only make us all uncomfortable.

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:09.630
And so, about your new foreman...

00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:11.250
I was hoping I could ask you, Marilla.

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:12.250
What?!

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:13.500
Really?

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:15.130
Marilla? Our foreman?
Then we've nothing to worry about!

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:17.130
No, no, no! Wait a minute! Just hold on!

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.880
No! I can't be foreman!

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.830
Then who else could I ask to do it?

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:26.170
If Marilla won't do it, I will!

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:28.580
And I'll give everyone three lunch breaks!

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:29.920
Then I volunteer!

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:31.000
I'll double our wages!

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.630
I'll turn the mill into a flower garden!

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:34.580
Fine! I'll do it!

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:35.540
Hooray!

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:36.630
We're counting on you, Marilla!

00:21:36.630 --> 00:21:37.750
Foreman Marilla!

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:41.460
But I won't be as forgiving as Priscilla!

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:43.000
Get ready to work!

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:44.790
Yes, ma'am!

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:48.670
Priscilla!

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:52.130
Would you tell Chieko something for me?

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:57.250
I don't really know what's going on in her life...

00:21:58.000 --> 00:21:59.670
But, um...

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:06.080
Tell her, "Don't let it beat you."

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:08.170
I will.

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:16.960
You think the girls at the laundry mill
will get on without us?

00:22:20.330 --> 00:22:21.420
I do.

00:22:21.790 --> 00:22:24.170
They are now strong enough.

00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:26.880
I'm certain they'll be fine.

00:22:28.330 --> 00:22:29.500
Let's go.

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:30.830
Yes, ma'am.
